    "blurb": "Read-only access to cluster data",
    "overview": "Query process instances, incidents, user tasks, audit logs and more from the Camunda Orchestration Cluster API v2. Read-only and OAuth 2.0 secured, it is the drop-in replacement for the deprecated Operate Connector.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Get read-only visibility into your orchestration cluster",
    "splashDescription": "The Orchestration Cluster API connector gives your BPMN processes read-only access to the Camunda Orchestration Cluster REST API (v2), the successor to the deprecated Operate API. It works against both SaaS and Self-Managed Camunda clusters and supports operations across every major entity in the cluster, including process instances, process definitions, element instances, incidents, variables, user tasks, jobs, decision instances, decision definitions, decision requirements, batch operations and their items, message subscriptions, correlated message subscriptions, audit logs, authorizations, groups, roles, tenants and mapping rules. If you are currently using the Camunda Operate connector, this connector is its direct replacement and covers the same ground against the newer Orchestration Cluster API v2.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/861093/overview/img5360630458727025036.png?5956cf7b7a2ffe0358dd9fda6837207c",
